# brainyard-jolt (`byj`) environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you use:  cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is gitignored — never commit real secrets. This template is safe to commit.
#
# Where it is read from (main.clj `env-fn`): the nearest `.env` walking up from
# the working directory, else ~/.brainyard/.env. A variable already set in the
# real environment wins over the file. Lines are `KEY=value` (an `export`
# prefix and surrounding quotes are allowed); `#` starts a comment line.
#
# Unlike brainyard's `by` wrapper, nothing here is exported into the process
# environment: the port reads the file itself, so a variable only takes effect
# where the port looks it up (credentials, config keys, MCP `${VAR}`s). The
# exceptions are marked below.
#
# You only need credentials for the provider you use. Two need no key at all:
#   claude-code  — drives the local `claude` CLI and its own login (the default
#                  when no key below is set)
#   ollama       — local models on http://localhost:11434 (no key)

# ── Which provider, when -p is not given ────────────────────────────────────
# main.clj `default-provider`: the first of these that has credentials —
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN → anthropic
#   OPENAI_API_KEY                            → openai
#   FREELLM_API_KEY and FREELLM_BASE_URL      → freellm
#   otherwise                                 → claude-code
# `-p NAME -m MODEL`, or `/model` in a session, picks one explicitly.

# ── LLM provider credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# OpenAI-compatible endpoint override (provider :openai): a proxy or gateway
# speaking the OpenAI API. Unset means https://api.openai.com/v1.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# Anthropic via a gateway or proxy (provider :anthropic). Two independent knobs:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN  a bearer credential, sent as `Authorization: Bearer`
#                         instead of `x-api-key`. Consulted only when
#                         ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset, so setting both keeps the
#                         API key.
#   ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL    where the Messages API lives. Unset means
#                         https://api.anthropic.com/v1.
#
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# Free or self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint (provider :freellm).
# FREELLM_BASE_URL is any OpenAI-compatible /v1 base; FREELLM_API_KEY is sent as
# a Bearer token when set. Use as: byj -p freellm -m auto "…"
FREELLM_BASE_URL=
FREELLM_API_KEY=

# ── AWS / Bedrock (provider :bedrock) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Calls go through the `aws` CLI, which resolves profiles, SSO and regions
# itself. AWS_PROFILE is passed as `--profile`; AWS_REGION picks the region
# (us-east-1 when unset).
AWS_PROFILE=
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
#
# Static keys instead of a profile are read by the `aws` CLI from the REAL
# environment only — export them in your shell rather than setting them here.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# ── Config keys ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every config key can be set here as BY_<KEY>: upper case, `-` as `_`, a
# trailing `?` dropped (config.clj `env-name`) — so :max-iterations is
# BY_MAX_ITERATIONS and :recap? is BY_RECAP. This layer outranks the config
# files AND the command-line flags (default < user < project < flags < env,
# RFC-013); `byj --print-config` shows each key's value and where it came
# from, and `/config` lists them by family. A few worth knowing:
#
# BY_WORKING_DIR=                  # where tools work (default: the process cwd)
# BY_PROJECT_DIR=                  # where .brainyard/ lives (default: the git root above it)
# BY_PERMISSION_MODE=auto          # auto | auto-approve | ask-each-time | deny-by-default
# BY_OUTPUT_STYLE=default          # default | concise | explanatory (how much a turn shows)
# BY_MAX_ITERATIONS=20             # iteration ceiling for one turn
# BY_CACHE_TTL=5m                  # 5m | 1h — prompt-cache lifetime (1h bills writes at 2x)
# BY_COMPACTION_SUMMARY=true       # tier-2 compaction: summarise old iterations before dropping
# BY_MCP_REGISTRY=true             # let /mcp find also search the MCP Registry (network)
# BY_ENABLE_MOUSE=true             # the full-screen renderer's mouse reporting

# ── Container detection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With :permission-mode auto, a container approves tool calls and anything else
# asks (permission.clj `resolve-mode`). The container is detected by
# /.dockerenv, or by BY_CONTAINER=1 — read from the REAL environment, not this
# file, so set it in the container's environment.
# BY_CONTAINER=1

# ── macOS sandbox (--sandbox) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relaunch under a seatbelt profile: writes contained to ~/.brainyard, the
# working dir, $TMPDIR and /tmp (RFC-012). Each matches a --sandbox* flag.
# BY_SANDBOX=1                     # sandbox without passing --sandbox
# BY_SANDBOX_PROFILE=/path/to.sb   # a seatbelt profile file instead of the generated one
# BY_SANDBOX_ALLOW_WRITE=/a,/b     # extra writable directories, comma-separated
# BY_SANDBOX_NO_NETWORK=1          # deny network (LLM calls will fail)
# BY_SANDBOX_SELF=target/byj   # the command that relaunches this program, when it cannot be worked out

# ── MCP servers (/mcp) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A server spec's `${VAR}` in :args and :env is filled from here when it starts,
# so config.edn names a token without holding it (RFC-024). The catalogue
# entries (`/mcp find`) that need one:
#
# github — a personal access token with the scopes you need (e.g. repo)
# GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#
# postgres — the database to query (read-only)
# POSTGRES_CONNECTION_STRING=postgresql://user:pass@localhost:5432/db
#
# redis — defaults to redis://localhost:6379 when unset
# REDIS_URL=
#
# filesystem — the directory it may read and write; defaults to the working dir
# MCP_FILESYSTEM_ROOT=
#
# google-workspace (Gmail, Calendar) — a Google Cloud OAuth client; the first
# start opens a browser consent. Passed into the server's environment.
# GCP_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GCP_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# A server from the MCP Registry names what it needs in `/mcp NAME`; set it here
# the same way.

# ── GitHub CLI (gh) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The `bash` tool runs `gh` with the REAL environment, so export GH_TOKEN in
# your shell if the agent should use gh; a value here is not passed on.
# GH_TOKEN=
